# claudebox settings for this machine. Copy to "config" next to this file:
#
#   cp ~/.claudebox/config.example ~/.claudebox/config
#
# Sourced as shell by the launcher, so it is plain assignments (and anything
# else bash accepts, though there is rarely a reason). The environment wins over
# what is set here, so a one-off override still works:
#
#   BOX_WORKSPACE_HOST=/mnt/elsewhere claudebox
#
# "config" is gitignored: it describes this machine, not the box's design.

# --- the workspace ---------------------------------------------------------

# Where the box sees the source tree. Leave this alone unless you have a reason:
# everything in the box, and every path it prints, is built on it.
#BOX_WORKSPACE="${HOME}/Projects"

# The host directory bound there. Defaults to BOX_WORKSPACE, which keeps paths
# identical inside and out. Point it elsewhere to work on a tree that lives on
# another drive -- an external SSD, or a removable drive carried between
# machines -- while the box still sees a plain ~/Projects:
#BOX_WORKSPACE_HOST=/media/dizzy/transfer/Projects

# --- everything else -------------------------------------------------------

# The box user and its ids. Default to yours; changing them means rebuilding.
#BOX_USER="$(id -un)"
#BOX_UID="$(id -u)"
#BOX_GID="$(id -g)"

# Which host home the launcher reads optional config from (~/.gitconfig,
# opencode's config and credentials).
#BOX_HOST_HOME="${HOME}"

# The mkcert root CA to trust, so https://*.ddev.site validates in the box.
#BOX_MKCERT_CA="${HOME}/.local/share/mkcert/rootCA.pem"

# Which DDEV project's database is reachable as db:3306. Auto-detected when
# exactly one project is running; pin it when several are.
#BOX_DDEV_PROJECT=matomo

# AppArmor profile for the rootless dind sidecar. On Ubuntu 24.04 the named
# profile is required -- see apparmor/claudebox-dind. On a host with no AppArmor
# confinement, "unconfined" is right.
#BOX_DIND_APPARMOR=unconfined

# --- the remote test runner -------------------------------------------------

# Set by "claudebox runner add <host:port> <token> <fingerprint>", which is the
# line the other machine's "claudebox-runner" prints when it starts. They are
# handed to the runner-relay container and to nothing else -- the box itself
# never sees the address, the token or the fingerprint, which is what keeps a
# remote runner from being a hole in the egress sandbox.
#
# Edit them by re-running "claudebox runner add" rather than by hand; the
# fingerprint has to match the runner's current certificate exactly.
#BOX_RUNNER=192.168.1.42:7998
#BOX_RUNNER_TOKEN=...
#BOX_RUNNER_FINGERPRINT=AA:BB:...

# --- on a RUNNER machine ----------------------------------------------------
#
# The same file is read by "claudebox-runner" on the machine that runs the
# tests, where these are the settings that apply instead. A machine is normally
# one or the other, so these sit unused on this one.

# The port the runner listens on, and where it keeps its copy of the source
# (a path inside its workspace volume, not on that machine's disk).
#BOX_RUNNER_PORT=7998
#BOX_RUNNER_WORKSPACE=/home/dizzy/Projects
